comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-24T21:40:02.778Z",codex-agent,"Oriented context, searched existing hygiene work, and read the complete tracker. Checking every original in-progress and open item against PR title/body/commits, delivery links and acceptance. The owner authorizes evidence-backed closure in this sweep. Ambiguous claims remain open; no PR merge or history rewrite."
  "2026-10-24T21:53:34.413Z",codex-agent,Delivery closures are complete except pm-github-f1ev and pm-github-2o9k. The repo-pinned SDK refuses both records with project_runtime_item_format_incompatible because existing linked tests retain updated_by/updated_at metadata while the consumer floor is 2026.10.5. No evidence or history was removed. A prepared peer/manifest 2026.10.10 floor proposal passes 4/4 compatibility checks outside this tracker and awaits owner authorization because it changes consumer support. General bounded aggregation returns to open. Release this sweep claim while the compatibility decision is pending.
  "2026-10-24T21:54:53.731Z",codex-agent,"Local tracker verification passed: repository changelog generation and consistency check, pinned strict health with required merge drivers under isolated Git identity, changed-item history verification, independent original-history prefix checks and linked git diff --check. The audit claim is released. Remaining in-progress count: 2. Any preserved guarded records and the required owner compatibility decision are explicitly listed in the PR. No production function changed, so source-function revert proof is inapplicable; per-item merged ancestry and lifecycle/history checks are the evidence. The PR will carry the full before/after/evidence table. Complete npm/Bun release checks and native platform checks run in PR CI; their final outcome is reported separately, without treating queued or skipped checks as approval."
